  "notes": [
    "Divisional Commander always carries 'A Marshal's baton in every knapsack'.",
    "0 to 2 Old Guard Infantry Brigades: 0-1 Old Guard regiment (1-2 battalions), 0-2 Middle Guard regiments (only one brigade may take two).",
    "0 to 2 Young Guard Infantry Brigades: 1-3 Young Guard regiments; one brigade may add a Fusilier-Grenadier and a Fusilier-Chasseur regiment.",
    "0 to 1 Imperial Guard Heavy Cavalry Brigade: up to 1 Grenadiers à Cheval and up to 1 Empress Dragoons regiment.",
    "0 to 3 Imperial Guard Light Cavalry Brigades: Chasseurs à Cheval de la Garde or Polish/Dutch 'Red' Lancers, plus Tiny Mamelukes or Small Gendarmes d'Elite.",
    "Imperial Guard Artillery Reserve: up to 5 Old Guard Horse batteries or 4 Young Guard Horse batteries, plus 1 Old Guard Heavy Foot battery if 8 infantry battalions taken.",
    "0 to 1 Italian Brigade (1-2 Velite battalions, 0-1 Tiny Italian Gardes d'Honneur) and Marines/Engineers battalion may attach to any Infantry Brigade.",
    "Allies: an Imperial Guard army may take 50% allies from the main French list, plus 25% from any other allied list."
  ]
}
